    "note": "GS724TPv2 data sheet: \"24 PoE+ (190W PoE budget)\" and \"24 x 1000BASE-T PoE+ Copper ports, 2 x 1000BASE-X Dedicated Fiber SFP ports\" - the port table this file carries. The 192 W figure this entry used to quote belongs to the 2007 GS724TPv1 sheet (802.3af, 15.4 W per port, 225 W max supply, 2 combo copper/SFP slots); the current revision is 190 W. 24 x 30 W = 720 W of port ceiling against 190 W, so the budget is the limit."
  },
  "notes": "Vendor figures from the GS724TPv2 data sheet: **24 PoE+ ports**, a **190 W power budget**, 2 dedicated SFP slots. **190 W over 24 powered ports is 7.9 W average** - six 30 W 802.3at devices exhaust it, so a camera plan needs the budget arithmetic before the port count. Two revisions carry the name: the 2007 GS724TPv1 is 802.3af at 15.4 W per port on a 192 W budget with 2 combo copper/SFP slots, and this entry is the PoE+ layout (dedicated SFP) at 190 W. The 192 W figure was imported from the v1 sheet and sat beside 802.3at ports."
